hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17676","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us: Abu 'Ushshanah narrated to me that Sufyan ibn Wahb al-Khawlani narrated to him that he was beneath the shade of the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Farewell Hajj, or that a man narrated that to him, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preaching. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have I conveyed? We thought he meant us, so we said: Yes. Then he repeated it three times, and said in what he said: A stroll in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it, and a morning expedition in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it. And the believer is inviolable to the believer: his honor, his wealth, and his life, inviolable as the sanctity of this day."
